gQE(){return"The text is written in a mannered, clear, seriffed, round uncial script in Greek, arranged in one column with 14 lines per page. The scribe used carbon ink, wrote with bilinear letters without rulings or prickings, employing nomina sacra and a cipher for numbers."},
gQC(){return u.I},
gQy(){return"From a textological perspective, uncial exhibits strong affinities with the Alexandrian text-type \u2013 showing notable agreement with Codex Sinaiticus and Papyrus 47 \u2013 although its fragmentary nature prevents a definitive classification."},
